+# Working on Umpire
+
+Umpire is an independent framework workspace. Keep reusable authoring, checkers,
+protocols, runtime, host and tooling here; system Models, API acquisition and
+realizations belong to their consumers. Kettle is the independent reference.
+
+Before changing authoring or checker behavior, read [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) and the
+nearest crate's documentation. Before changing guest compilation, identity or
+freshness, read [GUEST_BUILDS.md](GUEST_BUILDS.md) and
+[the native driver contract](dev/guest-driver/README.md). Before changing wire or
+host behavior, read [the protocol contract](protocol/proto/README.md) and
+[the Go host guide](hosts/go/README.md).
+
+Use the root Make aliases in [README.md](README.md) for framework checks. Keep
+command semantics in `dev/xtask` and `dev/guest-driver`; scripts and Make only
+bootstrap or delegate. Preserve the original caller's Cargo home, workspace,
+relative outputs and explicit target overrides across tool launches.
+
+The runtime library owns reusable dispatch; guest crates choose and export their
+Model at build time. Build generic wasm locally and keep it out of Git and LFS.
+Preserve protocol package names, field tags and ABI unless the change explicitly
+requires a coordinated protocol migration. Regenerate Go from owning schemas
+with `scripts/proto-go.sh`; keep generated changes together with their inputs.
+
+Retain deterministic fixture and mutation controls when changing semantics.
+Refresh goldens only for an intended behavior change and explain the changed
+observations. Report actual commands, source revision and backend mode: historical
+receipts and a default gate that skips TLC do not establish current required-backend
+validation. Record timing overruns against the existing soft budgets.
