+# Umpire design
+
+Umpire checks authored state machines and judges observations from real systems.
+The framework owns the authoring language, shared admission and typed IR, checkers,
+wire protocols, transactional runtime, Go transport/Runner and testing tools.
+Consumers own their Models, API descriptor acquisition, realizations, guests and
+system connections. [Kettle](reference/kettle/README.md) is a complete independent
+reference. Consumer checkout wiring is described in
+[the interface map](docs/consumer-interface.md).
+
+## Authoring and checking
+
+`author/umpire` is the author facade over DSL, suite and catalog. A `#[machine]`
+module declares its Model, fixed World parameters, actors, transitions and claims.
+The World is selected explicitly; its generated constructor assigns fields rather
+than validating arbitrary domain constraints. The [README](README.md#model-authoring)
+contains the executable authoring example.
+
+`front` reads declarations and the admitted body subset once inside the macro.
+`ir` carries the typed tree and source locations. The macro generates executable
+Rust and embeds the admitted tree off wasm. Structural errors refuse compilation;
+unsupported body syntax produces a located diagnostic and refuses emission while
+native checking remains available. A new IR field participates in derived
+constructor printing rather than a separate handwritten registration table.
+
+The native checker explores compiled Model bodies. Its interpreter evaluates the
+embedded tree as a differential check; compiled execution remains the default.
+The TLA emitter binds that same tree to the selected World, starts and catalog.
+TLC checks emitted modules independently of native graph exploration. Agreement
+requires complete reached sets and every selected verdict to agree, then typed
+replay checks counterexamples through compiled Model steps. A cut native graph
+cannot certify agreement. The common front end is a shared failure boundary;
+compiled replay and differential execution provide distinct cross-checks.
+
+Authored `stay!()` preserves a self-loop; `reject!` records a rejected outcome.
+Unchanged ordinary handlers remain disabled. Progress plans retain exact catalog
+membership and concrete fair actions for the selected World. World-selected
+assumptions and bounded optional values retain the admission limits documented in
+[README.md](README.md).
+
+## Backends and process ownership
+
+`backends/process` owns bounded native process execution, Java admission, capture
+and scratch cleanup for TLC and Apalache. The TLA emitter owns emission and typed
+values, rather than child supervision. Linux adopts and cleans up descendants;
+Darwin prevents descendants and refuses execution as root. Other platforms refuse.
+The audited syscall subtree is the local unsafe exception; safe crate roots retain
+`forbid(unsafe_code)`. Java heap settings and polled file limits are not kernel
+resource caps.
+
+TLC execution is required by `make validate`; default `make check` reports its
+skipped backend mode. Apalache is independently opt-in with
+`UMPIRE_APALACHE=require`. Backend refusal, incomplete dumps and disagreement are
+failures, rather than successful checks. Tool versions and checksums remain owned
+by the local configuration and installer code.
+
+## Runtime, guest and host
+
+`protocol/runtime` is an export-free reusable library for messages, transactional
+dispatch and ABI support. A guest crate chooses its concrete Model/realization at
+build time and invokes `export_guest!`. The stock guest selects the independent
+Kettle control; it is not a runtime plugin loader or a universal Model binary.
+The three application exports and ownership rules are defined by
+[the protocol contract](protocol/proto/README.md). Generic wasm is source-built,
+uncommitted and uses no Git LFS. See [GUEST_BUILDS.md](GUEST_BUILDS.md).
+
+One fresh Host belongs to a Run. The Go host owns transport and admission; the
+Runner serializes calls, drives a system-specific Driver, and records exact Model
+requests and responses. The Model owns Propose, Judge and Answer decisions.
+Explained behavior covers the recorded observations and termination budget, rather
+than every possible future. Refusal and Driver faults remain distinct from a
+Model's unexplained verdict. Replay uses a fresh same-hash/version Host and exact
+ordered evidence without external system I/O; redacted evidence cannot replay.
+The authoritative Run schema is
+[run.proto](protocol/proto/umpire/run/v1/run.proto).
+
+Generic annotation catalogs and realization envelopes remain framework-owned.
+System API acquisition and semantic catalog declarations remain consumer-owned;
+Kettle exercises descriptor-driven generation without a system extension.
+
+## Historical decisions and measurements
+
+The original extraction checkpoint is source `c88fdc5506`. The selected framework
+was exported with relevant Rust history; original `model/DESIGN.md`,
+`model/GUEST_BUILDS.md` and `model/design/` documents belonged to that source
+repository. Historical source IDs and evidence paths refer to that repository,
+not required standalone inputs. The original source repository was shallow at 2026-02-05, so earlier ancestry
+was unavailable during extraction; no missing ancestry is a build prerequisite.
+This document retains the generic decisions; system live-conformance obligations
+remain with their consumers.
+
+These observations establish only their named historical checkpoints. They are
+not benchmarks or validation of the extracted/adapted checkout.
+
+| Original checkpoint | Observation and limit |
+| --- | --- |
+| fn-210, 2026-10-18 | Stock Rust 1.99.1 wasm32-wasip1 Kettle on wazero 1.12.0 / Go 1.27.0, CGO disabled, matched native trait report and ordered rows: 81 starts, 283 states, 424 rows, depth 62. This predates the attribute surface. |
+| fn-238.4, `0bbeb1ff35` | Warm combined `make model-time`: 47.592 s gate, 7.272 s inner loop; default backend mode. These were original combined-workspace receipts. |
+| fn-238.9 derived printing | Required-TLC combined gate: 532.677 s (60 s target missed), inner loop 9.272 s (10 s target met). A prior cold attempt timed out at 600 s. This is not a steady-state comparison with default runs. |
+| fn-238.6, 2026-10-24 | Loaded-host interpreter pair medians 1.94× Kettle and 1.77× wide-shape compiled cost; Kettle upper quartile 2.01× and wide tail 3.3×. The proposed switch criteria were unmet; compiled remained default. Set construct cost remained unmeasured. |
+
+Original provenance: `model/design/rust-verdict-measurements.md` retains the
+2026-10-19 source, editor checks and reproduction commands;
+`model/DESIGN.md` retains backend/authoring receipts and their limitations.
+[Guest provenance](GUEST_BUILDS.md#historical-reproduction-evidence) records the
+separate byte-identity history. New claims require commands and receipts bound to
+the current source and backend modes; extraction does not discharge performance
+or system live-evidence obligations.
