 ```
 
-Run the complete framework gate from this directory:
+Run commands from this checkout's root. Java is required for TLC and Apalache;
+the local mise configuration retains its Java pin. The gate provisions the pinned
+Go protobuf generators into `.bin/` and checksum-pinned backend tools into local
+ignored caches as needed; a cold run needs network access. Helpers disable
+implicit mise installation and fail if pinned tools are missing.
+
+| Command | Existing native operation |
+| --- | --- |
+| `make check` | `cargo xtask gate`: formatting, clippy, docs, tests, source boundaries, protobuf freshness, guest builds and both Go host suites |
+| `make fmt` | `cargo xtask fmt`: format Rust |
+| `make update` | `cargo xtask update`: refresh intended fixture and compile-test snapshots |
+| `make time` | `cargo xtask time`: gate plus edited-checker timing |
+| `make validate` | `cargo xtask validate`: timed TLC-required gate plus edited-checker timing and isolated standalone proof |
+
+Make bootstraps the existing native tools through `scripts/xtask.sh`. Installed
+pinned tools also support `mise exec -- cargo xtask <operation>` directly.
+The full gate disables quick-cache reads and cache reuse via `UMPIRE_QUICK_CACHE=0`
+and `UMPIRE_CACHE_DISABLE=1`. Default checks skip TLC execution; `make validate`
+requires it. Add `UMPIRE_APALACHE=require` to require Apalache too. Timing budgets
+are soft targets (60 s full gate, 10 s inner loop); overruns must be reported.
+
+For direct Cargo work:
 
 ```sh
-mise exec -- cargo xtask gate
+mise exec -- cargo build --workspace --locked
+mise exec -- cargo test --workspace --locked
+mise exec -- cargo check-all
+mise exec -- cargo doc-all
 ```
 
