@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Consumer interface
+
+All framework paths below are relative to the Umpire checkout root. A typical
+paired layout has sibling `umpire/` and consumer repositories. The framework
+builds alone; the consumer selects the actual local checkout explicitly.
+
+| Surface | Owner and consumer contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| Cargo workspace | Umpire owns `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, local pins, profiles and tools. Consumers own separate workspaces/locks and use sibling path dependencies onto the actual crate paths. |
+| Author facade | `author/umpire` (`umpire`); lower-level crates remain available under `author/`, `catalog/` and `backends/`. |
+| Runtime / schemas | `protocol/runtime` and `protocol/proto`; reusable dispatch and shared envelopes. Consumers own extension schemas, API acquisition and generated extension code. |
+| Generic Go module | `github.com/temporalio/umpire/hosts/go`, rooted at `hosts/go`; transport in `host`, loop in `runner`, generated packages in `gen/umpire`. |
+| Reference Go module | `github.com/temporalio/umpire/reference/kettle`, rooted at `reference/kettle`, with its own server, schemas and fixtures. |
+| Local Go selection | A consumer/parent `go.work` includes the actual `hosts/go` and consumer modules; preserve existing workspace entries. The reference module replaces the generic module with `../../hosts/go`. |
+| Generic generation | `bash scripts/proto-go.sh core` or `kettle`; both accept `--check`. Consumers generate their own extension descriptors from their owning schemas. |
+| Framework checks | Root `make check`, `fmt`, `update`, `time`, `validate` delegate to existing native operations. They check Umpire; consumers retain their additional gates. |
+| Guest build / freshness | Absolute Umpire `scripts/guest.sh` and `scripts/guest-freshness.sh`; invoke from the consumer Cargo workspace. Output paths and target overrides retain caller meaning. |
+| Generic artifacts | `scripts/tests/build-guests.sh` builds generic wasm and native parity reports under the selected target. No prebuilt generic wasm is published or committed. |
+| Consumer artifacts | The consumer owns its concrete guest crate, selected Model, output destination, embedding, freshness checks and real system/SDK tests. |
+
+For example, from a consumer's Cargo workspace with an explicitly configured
+absolute `UMPIRE_ROOT` pointing to this checkout:
+
+```sh
+bash "$UMPIRE_ROOT/scripts/guest.sh" my-system-guest build/my-system.wasm
+bash "$UMPIRE_ROOT/scripts/guest-freshness.sh" my-system-guest build/my-system.wasm
+```
+
+The native bootstrap reports its executable path on stdout:
+
+```sh
+helper=$(bash "$UMPIRE_ROOT/scripts/xtask.sh")
+"$helper" gate
+```
+
+Use absolute checkout paths at the seam. A missing local checkout must fail with
+setup instructions rather than substituting registry or cached framework code.
+Framework gate execution uses framework-owned roots; guest execution uses the
+original caller's manifest and lockfile. See [guest context](../GUEST_BUILDS.md#caller-context-and-output)
+and [native contracts](../dev/xtask/README.md).
+
+These are source-prepared interfaces. Current-pair generation, required-backend
+gates, fresh-target proofs and disposable Rust/Go edit red/green demonstrations
+remain admission evidence to collect after the validation hold ends.
