@@ -112,3 +112,15 @@ hash, protocol version, world, seed, ordered events and verdict. Each event embe
 replays against a fresh instance without a Driver. It is generated for Go only; no guest
 reads it. Its canonical bytes are Go's deterministic encoding, and its store key carries
 their SHA-256 outside the payload.
+
+## Generated-source boundary policy
+
+After regenerating core or Kettle Go descriptors with `scripts/proto-go.sh`, run
+protobuf freshness and `cargo xtask gate --stage source-boundary`. The boundary
+policy admits three serialized module-path lines by exact file path and SHA-256,
+with generated-header and raw-descriptor context checks. When generation changes
+one of those lines, review the schema and generated diff before updating its
+`descriptor_lines` entry in `dev/gate/policy/framework-boundary.txt`; hash the full
+line bytes without the newline. Other bytes remain subject to the boundary check.
+Keep generated output untouched when updating admission. The root license also
+has an exact-content hash exception so its original copyright stays intact.
